# Accepted portability hits. Generated by scripts/checks/portability.sh --update.
#
# Every line here is a reason someone else cannot run this repository.
# The list should only ever get SHORTER. If you are adding to it, you are
# adding a reason - say why in the commit message.
#
# file<TAB>kind<TAB>count
# apps/portal-next/checks/repo-roots.mjs holds 18 home-path hits ON PURPOSE.
# Every one is a FICTIONAL machine - /home/ada, /Users/ada, /opt/bothy - because
# the whole file tests that Bothy works on a checkout that is NOT this one. A
# path to somebody else's home in that file is the opposite of a portability
# problem, and rewriting them to /srv/x would make the cases unreadable.
# Excluding all of apps/*/checks/ instead would be too broad: checks/env.py once
# carried this node's real tailnet address, and this check is what found it.
apps/portal-next/checks/repo-roots.mjs	home-path	18
apps/portal-next/compose.yml	tailnet-ip	1
apps/portal-next/web/vite.config.ts	tailnet-ip	1
auth/compose.yml	tailnet-ip	2
